[speeches]

; Required header — removing or renaming this will break the file.

normal=3
1:mood:I'm doing all right, just out for a walk in this weather.
2:day:Pretty normal day so far, nothing special to report.
3:opinion:Your stand looks nice, I've walked by it a few times now.
4:feedback:Maybe a bit more shade over the counter would be nice on a hot day.
5:walkoff:I've had enough chatting. I'm going somewhere else!

nice=4
1:mood:Oh, I'm having a wonderful day, thank you so much for asking!
2:day:Just lovely so far! Chatting with you is one of the highlights, honestly.
3:opinion:I think your stand is absolutely charming, you should be proud of it.
4:feedback:Honestly? I can't think of a single thing to improve. It's perfect as is!
5:walkoff:I really wanted to stay and chat, but I simply must have that lemonade!

mean=2
1:mood:How do you think I'm doing? I'm standing in line, that's how.
2:day:My day's been fine until I had to wait around here.
3:opinion:It's a lemonade stand. What is there to like?
4:feedback:You could start by being faster.
5:walkoff:That's it! I'm done waiting. This is absolutely ridiculous!

desperate=2
1:mood:I'm dying of thirst, that's how I'm doing!
2:day:My day has been one long search for something to drink!
3:opinion:Looks great, but can we skip to the part where I get lemonade?
4:feedback:Faster service, please, before I collapse!
5:walkoff:I can't take it anymore! I'm finding water somewhere else!

charitable=4
1:mood:I'm well, thank you. Trying to do a little good today.
2:day:Busy day, there are folks down the street who could use a hand.
3:opinion:It's a sweet little stand, and I love supporting local kids like you.
4:feedback:Maybe consider a pay-it-forward cup for someone who can't afford one.
5:walkoff:I really must go. That family can't wait any longer!

group=4
1:mood:We're doing great, thanks for asking! All %group_size% of us.
2:day:Been a fun day out, and now we're ready for a treat.
3:opinion:We've heard great things about this place from friends.
4:feedback:Maybe a bigger line area, there are %group_size% of us waiting here!
5:walkoff:We've had enough chatting. We're going somewhere else!

returning=3
1:mood:I'm doing well, and even better now that I'm back here.
2:day:Good day so far, I've been looking forward to this stop.
3:opinion:I already love it, that's why I keep coming back.
4:feedback:Maybe a loyalty discount for regulars like me?
5:walkoff:I came back for lemonade, not a conversation. I'm leaving!

critic=4
1:mood:I'm well. I try to stay objective no matter my mood.
2:day:I've reviewed two other stands today. Yours is next.
3:opinion:Charming presentation, though I reserve judgment until I taste the product.
4:feedback:Consistency. That's what separates a good stand from a forgettable one.
5:walkoff:I'm going to have to mention the wait time in my review. Please, the cup.

elderly=4
1:mood:Oh, I'm doing just fine for an old soul like me, thank you for asking, dear.
2:day:Lovely day for a walk down memory lane, if you ask me.
3:opinion:This reminds me of the stand I used to run, right down to the smell of fresh lemons.
4:feedback:Perhaps a little chair for us older folks to rest while we wait?
5:walkoff:Oh dear, I really must be going now. My feet aren't what they used to be.

child=3
1:mood:I'm good! Well, kinda thirsty, but good!
2:day:It was fun! I rode my bike here!
3:opinion:It's cool! Do you have any flavors? I like strawberry but lemon is okay too I guess.
4:feedback:You should totally have more flavors, like strawberry!
5:walkoff:UGH! I'm telling my mom! I'm leaving!
